// URL-loaded customization: enableNewSplit
//
// Enables metadata-driven display set splitting: series instances are split
// into display sets by the @cornerstonejs/metadata split-rules engine
// (`useMetadataDisplaySet` customization), with the @cornerstonejs/metadata
// default rules. A rule with a `handler` name (video, ECG, whole slide, SEG,
// RTSTRUCT, parametric map, SR, encapsulated document, bulk annotation,
// chart, unsupported) gives its display sets to the SOP class handler of the
// mode that declares that name in `handlerNames`, so the specialized
// extensions of OHIF keep working unchanged. A handler of another extension
// for a private SOP class runs only when it declares `handlerNames` and a rule
// names it: the default `unsupported` rule takes every other instance (see
// "A SOP class handler of another extension" in displaySetSplitting.md).
//
// The default rules include `localizer`, which puts the localizer images of
// a CT, MR or PT series that also has other images into their own display set,
// and `mixedDimensionalityBValue`, which splits MR
// series mixing instances with and without DiffusionBValue into separate
// display sets (the DWI mixed-b-value issue), and `singleImageModality`, which
// makes one display set for each CR, DX or MG image, as the stack SOP class
// handler does. `split/singleImagesBySize.jsonc` groups those images by size.
//
// Load it with `?customization=split/enableNewSplit`.
//
// Custom rules are @cornerstonejs/metadata rule data (a map of name to
// test in `matches`, names in `groupBy` and `sortBy`, a rule `context`, and
// `attributes`) - see `split/scoutSeries.jsonc` for a complete example.
// `displaySetRules` is the registry, keyed by rule id: add a rule with
// `$merge`, or change a rule by its id. `displaySetRuleOrder` is the list of
// rule ids in evaluation order, with first-match-wins per instance: add,
// remove or replace an id with `$spliceById`, which takes a rule id as the
// position (`[["volume3d", 0, "myRule"]]` inserts before `volume3d`). A rule
// that the order does not name is not used. An instance that no rule claims
// goes to the SOP class handlers.
{
  "global": {
    "useMetadataDisplaySet": { "enabled": { "$set": true } }
  }
}
